This Directory contains zoo, fiz and booz for OSK / Microware C.All changes to the sources are either sorrounded by #ifdef OSK .. #endifor marked with /* -hcz */. Whenever possible, OSK-specific additions weredone in osk.c and oskfiz.i.For successfull compliation you will need varargs.h (by Bob Larson, included here), TOP's os9lib.l and Microware's make utility.Documentation has been moved to the Directory MAN. The formattedoutput of unformatted (suffix: .1) files has been added (suffix: .man).The executables (Directory CMDS) are compiled with OSK V 2.4. For olderversions, you will have to recompile them if you get a 'cio mismatch'error, or you might try the following patch:    1.  look for the string '**** cio traphandler mismatch ****' in the        code.    2.  $62 bytes before, you will find the following sequence:        $7609 $2683 $262e    3.  The lower byte in $7609 (the 09) must be replaced by a         number which is lower or equal to your cio's revision        (08 for OSK 2.3).    4.  don't forget to update the module CRC after your patch        has been done.I never tried this patch with zoo, but it worked well with gcc andother programs some months ago when I was still using 2.3.Zoo is Public Domain. The same is true for this OSK port. Look atthe file 'Copyright' for details.**** BE WARNED ****On some systems, this version sometimes (very rarely) aborted during unpacking (bus error). Running zoo with srcdbg on thesame system under the same circumstances yielded no error,zoo worked as expected.Hints are welcome. Currently, you may need srcdbg to unpack your archives.. :-((~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Heike C. Zimmerer                                       hcz@reto.stgt.sub.orgreto Industrieelektronik GmbH      Kornbergstr. 18           7000 Stuttgart 1~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~